IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore): s 4(1) -- the defined terms, and s 4(2).
-- (s 4(3) to (13) are in sg-interpretation.l4; "business day" is in sg-periods.l4, which counts the Act's periods;
-- "related corporation" is in sg-groups.l4, beside s 6 which it points at.)
--
-- ONE FUNCTION PER DEFINED TERM, in the order of the text, with the facts a person could state as typed inputs.
-- Each returns MAYBE BOOLEAN (or MAYBE of the thing defined) and means this, by the rule of 2026-10-29:
--   JUST TRUE  the term's meaning, as s 4(1) states it, is met;
--   JUST FALSE only where the definition says "means" (a closed definition) or says no in a flat negative ("does not include");
--   NOTHING    where the definition says "includes" (an open list) and the case is not on it.
-- Every branch that answers JUST FALSE carries `FALSE-kind` and the definition's own words; every NOTHING carries `NOTHING-kind`.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- A definition that points at another Act ("the Accountants Act 2004", "the Securities and Futures Act 2001", ...) is a function
-- whose input is the fact that the other Act's test is met: the other Act is not among the sources and is never read from memory.
-- A definition that points at a section of this Act that a later wave encodes (s 175, s 197(1), s 190, ...) takes that
-- section's answer as an input, named for the fact and the section.
--
-- "means ... and includes ...": a term the text defines with "includes" is an open list: on the list is JUST TRUE, off the list is NOTHING
-- (a marginal reading, NOTES.md). A term the text defines with "means" alone is closed: off the definition is JUST FALSE.

§ `Types that more than one definition uses`

-- The facts about a body that s 4(1) "corporation" and "foreign company" turn on.
DECLARE `s 4(1) body` HAS
    `it is a body corporate formed or incorporated or existing in Singapore or outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a company, corporation, society, association or other body incorporated outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an unincorporated society, association or other body which under the law of its place of origin may sue or be sued, or hold property in the name of the secretary or other officer of the body or association duly appointed for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has its head office or principal place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is incorporated in Singapore and declared by notification of the Minister in the Gazette to be a public authority, an instrumentality or agency of the Government, or a body corporate which is not incorporated for commercial purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a corporation sole` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a cooperative society` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a registered trade union` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a platform work association registered under the Platform Workers Act 2024` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN

-- What a person is, for s 4(1) "officer".
DECLARE `s 4(1) "officer" what the person is` IS ONE OF
    `s 4(1) "officer" a director of the corporation`
    `s 4(1) "officer" the secretary of the corporation`
    `s 4(1) "officer" a person employed in an executive capacity by the corporation`
    `s 4(1) "officer" a receiver and manager of any part of the undertaking of the corporation appointed under a power contained in an instrument`
    `s 4(1) "officer" a liquidator of a company appointed in a voluntary winding up`
    `s 4(1) "officer" a receiver who is not also a manager`
    `s 4(1) "officer" a receiver and manager appointed by the Court`
    `s 4(1) "officer" a liquidator appointed by the Court or by the creditors`
    `s 4(1) "officer" a judicial manager appointed under Part 7 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `s 4(1) "officer" anyone else`

-- What kind of person is being identified, for s 4(1) "identification".
DECLARE `s 4(1) "identification" kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `s 4(1) "identification" an individual issued with an identity card under the National Registration Act 1965`
    `s 4(1) "identification" an individual not issued with an identity card under that Act`
    `s 4(1) "identification" a person other than an individual formed or incorporated in Singapore`
    `s 4(1) "identification" a person other than an individual formed or incorporated outside Singapore and registered under Division 2 of Part 11`
    `s 4(1) "identification" a person other than an individual formed or incorporated outside Singapore and not registered under Division 2 of Part 11`

-- The kind of winding up, for s 4(1) "commencement of winding up".
DECLARE `s 4(1) "commencement of winding up" kind of winding up` IS ONE OF
    `s 4(1) "commencement of winding up" a winding up by the Court`
    `s 4(1) "commencement of winding up" a voluntary winding up`
    `s 4(1) "commencement of winding up" any other winding up`

§ `The definitions, in the order of s 4(1)`

-- src:1141 | “accounting corporation” means a company approved or
-- src:1142 | deemed to be approved as an accounting corporation under
-- src:1143 | the Accountants Act 2004;
@ref s 4(1) "accounting corporation" (src:1141-1143)
GIVEN `the company is approved, or deemed to be approved, as an accounting corporation under the Accountants Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "accounting corporation" the company is an accounting corporation` MEANS
    IF `the company is approved, or deemed to be approved, as an accounting corporation under the Accountants Act 2004`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“accounting corporation” means a company approved or deemed to be approved as an accounting corporation under the Accountants Act 2004;"


-- src:1145 | “accounting entity” means a public accountant, an accounting
-- src:1146 | corporation, an accounting firm or an accounting limited
-- src:1147 | liability partnership;
@ref s 4(1) "accounting entity" (src:1145-1147)
GIVEN `the person is a public accountant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an accounting corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an accounting firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an accounting limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "accounting entity" the person is an accounting entity` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a public accountant`
       OR `the person is an accounting corporation`
       OR `the person is an accounting firm`
       OR `the person is an accounting limited liability partnership`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“accounting entity” means a public accountant, an accounting corporation, an accounting firm or an accounting limited liability partnership;"


