       AND `the standards are applicable to companies and to foreign companies in respect of their operations in Singapore for the purposes of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Accounting Standards” means the accounting standards made or formulated by the Accounting Standards Committee under Part 3 of the Accounting Standards Act 2007 and applicable to companies and to foreign companies in respect of their operations in Singapore for the purposes of this Act;"


-- src:1174 | “accounts” means profit and loss accounts and balance sheets
-- src:1175 | and includes notes (other than auditors’ reports or directors’
-- src:1176 | reports) attached or intended to be read with any of those
-- src:1177 | profit and loss accounts or balance sheets;
@ref s 4(1) "accounts" (src:1174-1177)
GIVEN `the thing is a profit and loss account or a balance sheet` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a note attached or intended to be read with a profit and loss account or balance sheet` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the note is an auditors' report or a directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "accounts" the thing is within the word accounts` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a note attached or intended to be read with a profit and loss account or balance sheet` AND `the note is an auditors' report or a directors' report`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "includes notes (other than auditors' reports or directors' reports) attached or intended to be read with any of those profit and loss accounts or balance sheets"
    ELSE (IF `the thing is a profit and loss account or a balance sheet` OR `the thing is a note attached or intended to be read with a profit and loss account or balance sheet`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "means profit and loss accounts and balance sheets and includes notes ..." leaves the list open


