      `the person is principally responsible for the management and conduct of the business of the company, or part of the business of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "chief executive officer" the person is a chief executive officer of the company` MEANS
    IF    `the person is in direct employment of, or acting for or by arrangement with, the company`
       AND `the person is principally responsible for the management and conduct of the business of the company, or part of the business of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“chief executive officer”, in relation to a company, means any one or more persons, by whatever name described, who — (a) is in direct employment of, or acting for or by arrangement with, the company; and (b) is principally responsible for the management and conduct of the business of the company, or part of the business of the company, as the case may be;"


-- src:1265 | “commencement of winding up” —
-- src:1267 | (a) in a winding up by the Court, has the meaning given
-- src:1268 | by section 126 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:1269 | Dissolution Act 2018; and
-- src:1271 | (b) in a voluntary winding up, has the meaning given by
-- src:1272 | section 161(6) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:1273 | Dissolution Act 2018;
@ref s 4(1) "commencement of winding up" (src:1265-1273)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 4(1) "commencement of winding up" kind of winding up`
      `the date section 126 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 gives as the commencement of the winding up by the Court` IS A DATE
      `the date section 161(6) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 gives as the commencement of the voluntary winding up` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 4(1) "commencement of winding up" the date the winding up commences` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 4(1) "commencement of winding up" a winding up by the Court` THEN JUST `the date section 126 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 gives as the commencement of the winding up by the Court`           -- (a)
    WHEN `s 4(1) "commencement of winding up" a voluntary winding up` THEN JUST `the date section 161(6) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 gives as the commencement of the voluntary winding up`       -- (b)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the definition names a winding up by the Court and a voluntary winding up, and no other


-- src:1275 | “company” means a company incorporated under this Act or
-- src:1276 | under any corresponding previous written law;
@ref s 4(1) "company" (src:1275-1276)
GIVEN `the body is a company incorporated under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a company incorporated under a corresponding previous written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "company" the body is a company` MEANS
