-- src:1360 | “debenture” includes debenture stock, bonds, notes and any
-- src:1361 | other securities of a corporation whether constituting a
-- src:1366 | charge on the assets of the corporation or not, but does not
-- src:1367 | include —
-- src:1369 | (a) a cheque, letter of credit, order for the payment of
-- src:1370 | money or bill of exchange;
-- src:1372 | (b) subject to the regulations, a promissory note having a
-- src:1373 | face value of not less than $100,000 and having a
-- src:1374 | maturity period of not more than 12 months;
-- src:1376 | (c) for the purposes of the application of this definition to
-- src:1377 | a provision of this Act in respect of which any
-- src:1378 | regulations made thereunder provide that the word
-- src:1379 | “debenture” does not include a prescribed document
-- src:1380 | or a document included in a prescribed class of
-- src:1381 | documents, that document or a document included in
-- src:1382 | that class of documents, as the case may be;
@ref s 4(1) "debenture" (src:1360-1382)
GIVEN `the instrument is debenture stock, a bond, a note or any other security of a corporation, whether constituting a charge on the assets of the corporation or not` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a cheque, a letter of credit, an order for the payment of money or a bill of exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a promissory note` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the face value of the promissory note, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the maturity period of the promissory note, in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the regulations made under this Act change the terms on which a promissory note is excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a document that regulations made under this Act prescribe, for the provision in question, as one the word debenture does not include` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "debenture" the instrument is a debenture` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is a cheque, a letter of credit, an order for the payment of money or a bill of exchange`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include (a) a cheque, letter of credit, order for the payment of money or bill of exchange"
    ELSE (IF `the instrument is a document that regulations made under this Act prescribe, for the provision in question, as one the word debenture does not include`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) for the purposes of the application of this definition to a provision of this Act in respect of which any regulations made thereunder provide that the word debenture does not include a prescribed document ..., that document"
          ELSE (IF `the instrument is a promissory note` AND `the regulations made under this Act change the terms on which a promissory note is excluded`
                THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "(b) subject to the regulations, a promissory note having a face value of not less than $100,000 and having a maturity period of not more than 12 months" -- the regulations are not among the sources
                ELSE (IF    `the instrument is a promissory note`
                        AND `the face value of the promissory note, in Singapore dollars` AT LEAST 100000
                        AND `the maturity period of the promissory note, in months` AT MOST 12
                      THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) subject to the regulations, a promissory note having a face value of not less than $100,000 and having a maturity period of not more than 12 months"
                      ELSE (IF `the instrument is debenture stock, a bond, a note or any other security of a corporation, whether constituting a charge on the assets of the corporation or not`
                            THEN JUST TRUE
                            ELSE NOTHING))))   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "debenture includes debenture stock, bonds, notes and any other securities of a corporation" leaves the list open


