-- src:1390 | “director” includes any person occupying the position of
-- src:1391 | director of a corporation by whatever name called and
-- src:1392 | includes a person in accordance with whose directions or
-- src:1393 | instructions the directors or the majority of the directors of a
-- src:1394 | corporation are accustomed to act and an alternate or
-- src:1395 | substitute director;
@ref s 4(1) "director" (src:1390-1395)
GIVEN `the person occupies the position of director of the corporation, by whatever name called` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors or the majority of the directors of the corporation are accustomed to act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors or the majority of the directors act on advice the person gives in a professional capacity, and that is the only reason they follow the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an alternate or substitute director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "director" the person is within the word director` MEANS
    IF    `the person occupies the position of director of the corporation, by whatever name called`
       OR (    `the directors or the majority of the directors of the corporation are accustomed to act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions`
           AND (NOT `s 4(2) the person is regarded as one in accordance with whose directions the directors are accustomed to act` `the directors or the majority of the directors act on advice the person gives in a professional capacity, and that is the only reason they follow the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE))
       OR `the person is an alternate or substitute director`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "director includes any person occupying the position of director ... and includes a person in accordance with whose directions or instructions the directors ... are accustomed to act and an alternate or substitute director" leaves the list open; a person caught only by s 4(2) is not regarded as a director by that limb


