-- src:1400 | “electronic communication” means communication transmitted
-- src:1401 | (whether from one person to another, from one device to
-- src:1402 | another, from a person to a device or from a device to a
-- src:1403 | person) —
-- src:1405 | (a) by means of a telecommunication system; or
-- src:1407 | (b) by other means but while in an electronic form,
-- src:1412 | such that it can (where particular conditions are met) be
-- src:1413 | received in legible form or be made legible following receipt
-- src:1414 | in non‑legible form;
@ref s 4(1) "electronic communication" (src:1400-1414)
GIVEN `the communication is transmitted (from one person to another, from one device to another, from a person to a device or from a device to a person) by means of a telecommunication system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the communication is transmitted (from one person to another, from one device to another, from a person to a device or from a device to a person) by other means but while in an electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it can (where particular conditions are met) be received in legible form or be made legible following receipt in non-legible form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "electronic communication" the communication is an electronic communication` MEANS
    IF (`the communication is transmitted (from one person to another, from one device to another, from a person to a device or from a device to a person) by means of a telecommunication system` OR `the communication is transmitted (from one person to another, from one device to another, from a person to a device or from a device to a person) by other means but while in an electronic form`) AND `it can (where particular conditions are met) be received in legible form or be made legible following receipt in non-legible form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“electronic communication” means communication transmitted (whether from one person to another, from one device to another, from a person to a device or from a device to a person) — (a) by means of a telecommunication system; or (b) by other means but while in an electronic form, such that it can (where particular conditions are met) be received in legible form or be made legible following receipt in non‑legible form;"


