       AND `the payment is made or given, directly or indirectly, to the director or auditor`
       AND `the payment is made or given by the company, or by a holding company or a subsidiary of the company`
       AND `the payment is made or given to the director or auditor in that capacity, or otherwise in connection with the affairs of the company or of the holding company or the subsidiary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“emoluments”, in relation to a director or auditor of a company, includes any fees, percentages and other payments made (including the money value of any allowances or perquisites) or consideration given, directly or indirectly, to the director or auditor by that company or by a holding company or a subsidiary of that company, whether made or given to the director or auditor in the director’s or auditor’s capacity as such or otherwise in connection with the affairs of that company or of the holding company or the subsidiary;"


-- src:1431 | “exempt private company” means —
