-- src:1463 | accordance with section 198;
@ref s 4(1) "financial year" (src:1451-1463)
GIVEN `the period is the period in respect of which the financial statements of the corporation are made up, whether that period is a year or not` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period is a financial year of the company as section 198 determines` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "financial year" the period is a financial year of the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the period is the period in respect of which the financial statements of the corporation are made up, whether that period is a year or not` OR (`the corporation is a company` AND `the period is a financial year of the company as section 198 determines`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“financial year” — (a) in relation to a corporation — means the period in respect of which the financial statements of the corporation is made up, whether that period is a year or not; and (b) in relation to a company — is also to be determined in accordance with section 198;"


-- src:1465 | “foreign company” means —
-- src:1467 | (a) a company, corporation, society, association or other
-- src:1468 | body incorporated outside Singapore; or
-- src:1470 | (b) an unincorporated society, association or other body
-- src:1471 | which under the law of its place of origin may sue or
-- src:1472 | be sued, or hold property in the name of the secretary
-- src:1473 | or other officer of the body or association duly
-- src:1474 | appointed for that purpose and which does not have
-- src:1475 | its head office or principal place of business in
-- src:1476 | Singapore;
@ref s 4(1) "foreign company" (src:1465-1476)
GIVEN body IS A `s 4(1) body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "foreign company" the body is a foreign company` MEANS
    IF    body's `it is a company, corporation, society, association or other body incorporated outside Singapore`
       OR (    body's `it is an unincorporated society, association or other body which under the law of its place of origin may sue or be sued, or hold property in the name of the secretary or other officer of the body or association duly appointed for that purpose`
           AND (NOT body's `it has its head office or principal place of business in Singapore`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“foreign company” means — (a) a company, corporation, society, association or other body incorporated outside Singapore; or (b) an unincorporated society, association or other body which under the law of its place of origin may sue or be sued, or hold property in the name of the secretary or other officer of the body or association duly appointed for that purpose and which does not have its head office or principal place of business in Singapore;"


-- src:1478 | “full name” or “name” means —
-- src:1480 | (a) in the case of an individual registered under the
-- src:1481 | National Registration Act 1965 — the name as it
-- src:1482 | appears in the latest identity card issued to that
-- src:1483 | individual under section 9 of that Act; or
-- src:1485 | (b) in the case of an individual not registered under the
-- src:1486 | National Registration Act 1965 — the name as it
-- src:1487 | appears in the latest passport issued to that individual
-- src:1488 | or such other similar evidence of identification as is
-- src:1489 | available;
@ref s 4(1) "full name" (src:1478-1489)
GIVEN `the individual is registered under the National Registration Act 1965` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name as it appears in the latest identity card issued to the individual under section 9 of that Act` IS A STRING
      `the name as it appears in the latest passport issued to the individual, or such other similar evidence of identification as is available` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 4(1) "full name" the full name of the individual` MEANS
    IF `the individual is registered under the National Registration Act 1965`
    THEN `the name as it appears in the latest identity card issued to the individual under section 9 of that Act`
    ELSE `the name as it appears in the latest passport issued to the individual, or such other similar evidence of identification as is available`


-- src:1493 | “identification” means —
-- src:1495 | (a) in the case of an individual issued with an identity
-- src:1496 | card under the National Registration Act 1965 — the
-- src:1497 | number of the individual’s identity card;
-- src:1501 | (b) in the case of an individual not issued with an identity
-- src:1502 | card under that Act — particulars of the individual’s
-- src:1503 | passport or such other similar evidence of identity as
-- src:1504 | is acceptable to the Registrar; and
-- src:1511 | (c) in the case of a person other than an individual —
-- src:1513 | (i) where the person is formed or incorporated in
-- src:1514 | Singapore — the unique entity number of the
-- src:1515 | person issued by a public agency;
-- src:1517 | (ii) where the person is formed or incorporated
-- src:1518 | outside Singapore and is registered under
-- src:1519 | Division 2 of Part 11 — the unique entity
-- src:1520 | number of the person issued by the Registrar;
-- src:1521 | or
-- src:1523 | (iii) where the person is formed or incorporated
-- src:1524 | outside Singapore and is not registered under
-- src:1525 | Division 2 of Part 11 — the identification
-- src:1526 | number or registration number of the person on
-- src:1527 | the corporate entity register (if applicable) of
-- src:1528 | the jurisdiction where the person is formed or
-- src:1529 | incorporated or any other similar evidence of
-- src:1530 | identity acceptable to the Registrar;
@ref s 4(1) "identification" (src:1493-1530)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 4(1) "identification" kind of person`
      `the number of the individual's identity card` IS A STRING
      `the particulars of the individual's passport, or of such other similar evidence of identity as is acceptable to the Registrar` IS A STRING
      `the unique entity number of the person issued by a public agency` IS A STRING
      `the unique entity number of the person issued by the Registrar` IS A STRING
      `the identification number or registration number of the person on the corporate entity register of the jurisdiction where it is formed or incorporated, or other similar evidence of identity acceptable to the Registrar` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 4(1) "identification" the identification of the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 4(1) "identification" an individual issued with an identity card under the National Registration Act 1965` THEN `the number of the individual's identity card`
    WHEN `s 4(1) "identification" an individual not issued with an identity card under that Act` THEN `the particulars of the individual's passport, or of such other similar evidence of identity as is acceptable to the Registrar`
    WHEN `s 4(1) "identification" a person other than an individual formed or incorporated in Singapore` THEN `the unique entity number of the person issued by a public agency`
    WHEN `s 4(1) "identification" a person other than an individual formed or incorporated outside Singapore and registered under Division 2 of Part 11` THEN `the unique entity number of the person issued by the Registrar`
    WHEN `s 4(1) "identification" a person other than an individual formed or incorporated outside Singapore and not registered under Division 2 of Part 11` THEN `the identification number or registration number of the person on the corporate entity register of the jurisdiction where it is formed or incorporated, or other similar evidence of identity acceptable to the Registrar`


-- src:1534 | “liquidator” includes the Official Receiver when acting as the
-- src:1535 | liquidator of a corporation;
@ref s 4(1) "liquidator" (src:1534-1535)
GIVEN `the person is the Official Receiver acting as the liquidator of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "liquidator" the person is within the word liquidator` MEANS
    IF `the person is the Official Receiver acting as the liquidator of a corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“liquidator” includes the Official Receiver when acting as the liquidator of a corporation;"


-- src:1537 | “limited company” means a company limited by shares or by
-- src:1538 | guarantee or, prior to the expiry of the period of 2 years as
-- src:1539 | specified in section 17(6), a company limited both by shares
-- src:1540 | and guarantee;
@ref s 4(1) "limited company" (src:1537-1540)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the period of 2 years specified in section 17(6) has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "limited company" the company is a limited company` MEANS
    CONSIDER liability
    WHEN `limited by shares` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `limited by guarantee` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `limited by shares and by guarantee` THEN
        (IF `the period of 2 years specified in section 17(6) has expired`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or, prior to the expiry of the period of 2 years as specified in section 17(6), a company limited both by shares and guarantee"
         ELSE JUST TRUE)
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "limited company means a company limited by shares or by guarantee or, prior to the expiry ..., a company limited both by shares and guarantee" (a "means" definition; an unlimited company is none of these)


-- src:1542 | “limited liability partnership” has the meaning given by
-- src:1543 | section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005;
@ref s 4(1) "limited liability partnership" (src:1542-1543)
GIVEN `the partnership is a limited liability partnership as section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005 gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "limited liability partnership" the partnership is a limited liability partnership` MEANS
    IF `the partnership is a limited liability partnership as section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005 gives that meaning`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“limited liability partnership” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005;"


-- src:1545 | “listed”, in relation to a company or corporation, means a
-- src:1546 | company or corporation that has been admitted to the official
-- src:1547 | list of an approved exchange in Singapore and has not been
-- src:1548 | removed from that official list;
@ref s 4(1) "listed" (src:1545-1548)
GIVEN `the company or corporation has been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company or corporation has been removed from that official list` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "listed" the company or corporation is listed` MEANS
    IF    `the company or corporation has been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore`
       AND (NOT `the company or corporation has been removed from that official list`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“listed”, in relation to a company or corporation, means a company or corporation that has been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore and has not been removed from that official list;"


-- src:1550 | “lodged” means lodged under this Act or any corresponding
-- src:1551 | previous written law;
@ref s 4(1) "lodged" (src:1550-1551)
GIVEN `the document is lodged under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is lodged under a corresponding previous written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "lodged" the document is lodged` MEANS
    IF `the document is lodged under this Act` OR `the document is lodged under a corresponding previous written law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“lodged” means lodged under this Act or any corresponding previous written law;"


-- src:1553 | “marketable securities” means debentures, funds, stocks, shares
-- src:1554 | or bonds of any government or of any local authority or of
-- src:1555 | any corporation or society and includes any right or option in
-- src:1560 | respect of shares in any corporation and units in a collective
-- src:1561 | investment scheme within the meaning of section 2 of the
-- src:1562 | Securities and Futures Act 2001;
@ref s 4(1) "marketable securities" (src:1553-1562)
GIVEN `the thing is a debenture, fund, stock, share or bond of a government, a local authority, or a corporation or society` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a right or option in respect of shares in a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme within the meaning of section 2 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "marketable securities" the thing is within the marketable securities` MEANS
    IF    `the thing is a debenture, fund, stock, share or bond of a government, a local authority, or a corporation or society`
       OR `the thing is a right or option in respect of shares in a corporation`
       OR `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme within the meaning of section 2 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“marketable securities” means debentures, funds, stocks, shares or bonds of any government or of any local authority or of any corporation or society and includes any right or option in respect of shares in any corporation and units in a collective investment scheme within the meaning of section 2 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001;"


-- src:1564 | “minimum subscription”, in relation to any shares offered to the
-- src:1565 | public for subscription, means the amount stated in the
-- src:1566 | prospectus relating to the offer as the minimum amount
-- src:1567 | which in the opinion of the directors must be raised by the
-- src:1568 | issue of the shares so offered;
@ref s 4(1) "minimum subscription" (src:1564-1568)
GIVEN `the shares are offered to the public for subscription` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount stated in the prospectus relating to the offer as the minimum amount which in the opinion of the directors must be raised by the issue of the shares offered, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 4(1) "minimum subscription" the minimum subscription` MEANS
    IF `the shares are offered to the public for subscription`
    THEN JUST `the amount stated in the prospectus relating to the offer as the minimum amount which in the opinion of the directors must be raised by the issue of the shares offered, in Singapore dollars`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "minimum subscription, in relation to any shares offered to the public for subscription, means ..." says nothing of shares not so offered


-- src:1570 | “office copy”, in relation to any Court order or other Court
-- src:1571 | document, means a copy authenticated under the hand or seal
-- src:1572 | of the Registrar or other proper officer of the Court;
@ref s 4(1) "office copy" (src:1570-1572)
GIVEN `the copy is a copy of a Court order or other Court document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is authenticated under the hand or seal of the Registrar or other proper officer of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "office copy" the copy is an office copy` MEANS
    IF `the copy is a copy of a Court order or other Court document` AND `the copy is authenticated under the hand or seal of the Registrar or other proper officer of the Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“office copy”, in relation to any Court order or other Court document, means a copy authenticated under the hand or seal of the Registrar or other proper officer of the Court;"


-- src:1574 | “officer”, in relation to a corporation, includes —
-- src:1576 | (a) any director or secretary of the corporation or a
-- src:1577 | person employed in an executive capacity by the
-- src:1578 | corporation;
-- src:1580 | (b) a receiver and manager of any part of the undertaking
-- src:1581 | of the corporation appointed under a power contained
-- src:1582 | in any instrument; and
-- src:1584 | (c) any liquidator of a company appointed in a voluntary
-- src:1585 | winding up,
-- src:1587 | but does not include —
-- src:1589 | (d) any receiver who is not also a manager;
-- src:1591 | (e) any receiver and manager appointed by the Court;
-- src:1593 | (f) any liquidator appointed by the Court or by the
-- src:1594 | creditors; or
-- src:1596 | (g) a judicial manager appointed under Part 7 of the
-- src:1597 | Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018;
@ref s 4(1) "officer" (src:1574-1597)
GIVEN position IS A `s 4(1) "officer" what the person is`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "officer" the person is an officer of the corporation` MEANS
    CONSIDER position
    WHEN `s 4(1) "officer" a director of the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE                                                                   -- (a)
    WHEN `s 4(1) "officer" the secretary of the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE                                                                -- (a)
    WHEN `s 4(1) "officer" a person employed in an executive capacity by the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE                                   -- (a)
    WHEN `s 4(1) "officer" a receiver and manager of any part of the undertaking of the corporation appointed under a power contained in an instrument` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b)
    WHEN `s 4(1) "officer" a liquidator of a company appointed in a voluntary winding up` THEN JUST TRUE                                    -- (c)
    WHEN `s 4(1) "officer" a receiver who is not also a manager` THEN JUST FALSE                                                           -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include (d) any receiver who is not also a manager"
    WHEN `s 4(1) "officer" a receiver and manager appointed by the Court` THEN JUST FALSE                                                  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(e) any receiver and manager appointed by the Court"
    WHEN `s 4(1) "officer" a liquidator appointed by the Court or by the creditors` THEN JUST FALSE                                        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(f) any liquidator appointed by the Court or by the creditors"
    WHEN `s 4(1) "officer" a judicial manager appointed under Part 7 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(g) a judicial manager appointed under Part 7 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "officer, in relation to a corporation, includes (a) ..., (b) ..., (c) ..." leaves the list open


-- src:1599 | “Official Assignee” means the Official Assignee appointed
-- src:1600 | under section 16(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:1601 | Dissolution Act 2018 and includes a Deputy Official
-- src:1602 | Assignee, a Senior Assistant Official Assignee and an
-- src:1603 | Assistant Official Assignee;
@ref s 4(1) "Official Assignee" (src:1599-1603)
GIVEN `the person is the Official Assignee appointed under section 16(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a Deputy Official Assignee, a Senior Assistant Official Assignee or an Assistant Official Assignee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "Official Assignee" the person is within the words Official Assignee` MEANS
    IF    `the person is the Official Assignee appointed under section 16(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
       OR `the person is a Deputy Official Assignee, a Senior Assistant Official Assignee or an Assistant Official Assignee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“Official Assignee” means the Official Assignee appointed under section 16(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 and includes a Deputy Official Assignee, a Senior Assistant Official Assignee and an Assistant Official Assignee;"


-- src:1608 | “Official Receiver” means the Official Receiver appointed
-- src:1609 | under section 17(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:1610 | Dissolution Act 2018 and includes a Deputy Official
-- src:1611 | Receiver, a Senior Assistant Official Receiver and an
-- src:1612 | Assistant Official Receiver;
@ref s 4(1) "Official Receiver" (src:1608-1612)
GIVEN `the person is the Official Receiver appointed under section 17(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a Deputy Official Receiver, a Senior Assistant Official Receiver or an Assistant Official Receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "Official Receiver" the person is within the words Official Receiver` MEANS
    IF    `the person is the Official Receiver appointed under section 17(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
       OR `the person is a Deputy Official Receiver, a Senior Assistant Official Receiver or an Assistant Official Receiver`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“Official Receiver” means the Official Receiver appointed under section 17(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 and includes a Deputy Official Receiver, a Senior Assistant Official Receiver and an Assistant Official Receiver;"


-- src:1614 | “prescribed” means prescribed under this Act or by the rules;
@ref s 4(1) "prescribed" (src:1614-1614)
GIVEN `the matter is prescribed under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is prescribed by the rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "prescribed" the matter is prescribed` MEANS
    IF `the matter is prescribed under this Act` OR `the matter is prescribed by the rules`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“prescribed” means prescribed under this Act or by the rules;"


-- src:1616 | “principal register”, in relation to a company, means the register
-- src:1617 | of members of the company kept pursuant to section 190;
@ref s 4(1) "principal register" (src:1616-1617)
GIVEN `the register is the register of members of the company kept pursuant to section 190` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "principal register" the register is the principal register of the company` MEANS
    IF `the register is the register of members of the company kept pursuant to section 190`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“principal register”, in relation to a company, means the register of members of the company kept pursuant to section 190;"


-- src:1619 | “printed” includes typewritten or lithographed or reproduced by
-- src:1620 | any mechanical means;
@ref s 4(1) "printed" (src:1619-1620)
GIVEN `the thing is typewritten` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is lithographed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is reproduced by any mechanical means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "printed" the thing is within the word printed` MEANS
    IF `the thing is typewritten` OR `the thing is lithographed` OR `the thing is reproduced by any mechanical means`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“printed” includes typewritten or lithographed or reproduced by any mechanical means;"


-- src:1622 | “private company” means —
-- src:1624 | (a) any company which immediately prior to
-- src:1625 | 29 December 1967 was a private company under
-- src:1626 | the provisions of the repealed written laws;
-- src:1628 | (b) any company incorporated as a private company by
-- src:1629 | virtue of section 18; or
-- src:1631 | (c) any company converted into a private company
-- src:1632 | pursuant to section 31(1),
-- src:1634 | being a company which has not ceased to be a private
-- src:1635 | company under section 31 or 32;
@ref s 4(1) "private company" (src:1622-1635)
GIVEN `the company, immediately before 29 December 1967, was a private company under the repealed written laws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company was incorporated as a private company by virtue of section 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company was converted into a private company pursuant to section 31(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has ceased to be a private company under section 31 or 32` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "private company" the company is a private company` MEANS
    IF (`the company, immediately before 29 December 1967, was a private company under the repealed written laws` OR `the company was incorporated as a private company by virtue of section 18` OR `the company was converted into a private company pursuant to section 31(1)`) AND (NOT `the company has ceased to be a private company under section 31 or 32`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“private company” means — (a) any company which immediately prior to 29 December 1967 was a private company under the provisions of the repealed written laws; (b) any company incorporated as a private company by virtue of section 18; or (c) any company converted into a private company pursuant to section 31(1), being a company which has not ceased to be a private company under section 31 or 32;"


-- src:1637 | “profit and loss account” includes income and expenditure
-- src:1638 | account, revenue account or any other account showing the
-- src:1639 | results of the business of a corporation for a period;
@ref s 4(1) "profit and loss account" (src:1637-1639)
GIVEN `the account is an income and expenditure account or a revenue account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the account is any other account showing the results of the business of a corporation for a period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "profit and loss account" the account is within the words profit and loss account` MEANS
    IF    `the account is an income and expenditure account or a revenue account`
       OR `the account is any other account showing the results of the business of a corporation for a period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“profit and loss account” includes income and expenditure account, revenue account or any other account showing the results of the business of a corporation for a period;"


-- src:1641 | “prospectus” means any prospectus, notice, circular, material,
-- src:1642 | advertisement, publication or other document —
-- src:1644 | (a) inviting applications or offers from the public to
-- src:1645 | subscribe for or purchase; or
-- src:1647 | (b) offering to the public for subscription or purchase,
-- src:1649 | any shares in or debentures of, or any units of shares in or
-- src:1650 | debentures of, a corporation or proposed corporation, and
-- src:1651 | includes any document deemed to be a prospectus under
-- src:1652 | section 257 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001, but does
-- src:1653 | not include —
-- src:1658 | (c) a profile statement; or
-- src:1660 | (d) any material, advertisement or publication which is
-- src:1661 | authorised by section 251 (other than subsection (5))
-- src:1662 | of that Act;
@ref s 4(1) "prospectus" (src:1641-1662)
GIVEN `the document is a prospectus, notice, circular, material, advertisement, publication or other document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document invites applications or offers from the public to subscribe for or purchase, or offers to the public for subscription or purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document concerns shares in or debentures of, or units of shares in or debentures of, a corporation or proposed corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is deemed to be a prospectus under section 257 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is material, an advertisement or a publication authorised by section 251 (other than subsection (5)) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "prospectus" the document is a prospectus` MEANS
    IF ((`the document is a prospectus, notice, circular, material, advertisement, publication or other document` AND `the document invites applications or offers from the public to subscribe for or purchase, or offers to the public for subscription or purchase` AND `the document concerns shares in or debentures of, or units of shares in or debentures of, a corporation or proposed corporation`) OR `the document is deemed to be a prospectus under section 257 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001`) AND (NOT `the document is a profile statement`) AND (NOT `the document is material, an advertisement or a publication authorised by section 251 (other than subsection (5)) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“prospectus” means any prospectus, notice, circular, material, advertisement, publication or other document — (a) inviting applications or offers from the public to subscribe for or purchase; or (b) offering to the public for subscription or purchase, any shares in or debentures of, or any units of shares in or debentures of, a corporation or proposed corporation, and includes any document deemed to be a prospectus under section 257 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001, but does not include — (c) a profile statement; or (d) any material, advertisement or publication which is authorised by section 251 (other than subsection (5)) of that Act;"


