-- src:1668 | “public agency” means a public officer, an Organ of State or a
-- src:1669 | ministry or department of the Government, or a body or
-- src:1670 | authority established by or under any public Act to perform
-- src:1671 | or discharge a public function, or a member, an officer or
-- src:1672 | employee, or any department thereof;
@ref s 4(1) "public agency" (src:1668-1672)
GIVEN `the body is a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is an Organ of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a ministry or department of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a body or authority established by or under a public Act to perform or discharge a public function` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a member, an officer or an employee of any of these, or any department of any of these` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "public agency" the body is a public agency` MEANS
    IF    `the body is a public officer`
       OR `the body is an Organ of State`
       OR `the body is a ministry or department of the Government`
       OR `the body is a body or authority established by or under a public Act to perform or discharge a public function`
       OR `the body is a member, an officer or an employee of any of these, or any department of any of these`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“public agency” means a public officer, an Organ of State or a ministry or department of the Government, or a body or authority established by or under any public Act to perform or discharge a public function, or a member, an officer or employee, or any department thereof;"


