    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“unlimited company” means a company formed on the principle of having no limit placed on the liability of its members;" (a "means" definition; a company limited both by shares and by guarantee is neither, which s 4(1) "limited company" names as a third kind: fork F4 in NOTES.md)


