-- src:1766 | “voting share”, in relation to a body corporate, means an issued
-- src:1767 | share in the body corporate, not being —
-- src:1769 | (a) a share to which, in no circumstances, is there
-- src:1770 | attached a right to vote; or
-- src:1772 | (b) a share to which there is attached a right to vote only
-- src:1773 | in one or more of the following circumstances:
-- src:1775 | (i) during a period in which a dividend (or part of a
-- src:1776 | dividend) in respect of the share is in arrear;
-- src:1778 | (ii) upon a proposal to reduce the share capital of
-- src:1779 | the body corporate;
-- src:1781 | (iii) upon a proposal that affects rights attached to
-- src:1782 | the share;
-- src:1784 | (iv) upon a proposal to wind up the body corporate;
-- src:1786 | (v) upon a proposal for the disposal of the whole of
-- src:1787 | the property, business and undertakings of the
-- src:1788 | body corporate;
-- src:1790 | (vi) during the winding up of the body corporate.
@ref s 4(1) "voting share" (src:1766-1790)
GIVEN `the share is an issued share in the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no right to vote is attached to the share in any circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a right to vote is attached to the share only in one or more of these circumstances: a dividend (or part of a dividend) in respect of the share is in arrear; a proposal to reduce the share capital of the body corporate; a proposal that affects rights attached to the share; a proposal to wind up the body corporate; a proposal for the disposal of the whole of the property, business and undertakings of the body corporate; the winding up of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "voting share" the share is a voting share` MEANS
    IF    `the share is an issued share in the body corporate`
       AND (NOT `no right to vote is attached to the share in any circumstances`)
       AND (NOT `a right to vote is attached to the share only in one or more of these circumstances: a dividend (or part of a dividend) in respect of the share is in arrear; a proposal to reduce the share capital of the body corporate; a proposal that affects rights attached to the share; a proposal to wind up the body corporate; a proposal for the disposal of the whole of the property, business and undertakings of the body corporate; the winding up of the body corporate`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“voting share”, in relation to a body corporate, means an issued share in the body corporate, not being — (a) a share to which, in no circumstances, is there attached a right to vote; or (b) a share to which there is attached a right to vote only in one or more of the following circumstances: (i) during a period in which a dividend (or part of a dividend) in respect of the share is in arrear; (ii) upon a proposal to reduce the share capital of the body corporate; (iii) upon a proposal that affects rights attached to the share; (iv) upon a proposal to wind up the body corporate; (v) upon a proposal for the disposal of the whole of the property, business and undertakings of the body corporate; (vi) during the winding up of the body corporate."


-- src:1797 | (2) For the purposes of this Act, a person (A) is not regarded as a
-- src:1798 | person in accordance with whose directions or instructions the
-- src:1799 | directors or the majority of the directors of a corporation are
-- src:1804 | accustomed to act by reason only that the directors or the majority of
-- src:1805 | the directors act on advice given by A in a professional capacity.
@ref s 4(2) (src:1797-1805)
GIVEN `the directors or the majority of the directors act on advice the person gives in a professional capacity, and that is the only reason they follow the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(2) the person is regarded as one in accordance with whose directions the directors are accustomed to act` MEANS
    IF `the directors or the majority of the directors act on advice the person gives in a professional capacity, and that is the only reason they follow the person`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(2) For the purposes of this Act, a person (A) is not regarded as a person in accordance with whose directions or instructions the directors or the majority of the directors of a corporation are accustomed to act by reason only that the directors or the majority of the directors act on advice given by A in a professional capacity."
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection only carves an exception out of the definition; it says nothing where the directors follow the person for any other reason
